---
const questions = [
  { question: 'Are these gradient backgrounds free to download?', answer: 'Yes. Every gradient on FreeeGradients is free to download and use. You can copy CSS or export SVG, PNG and JPEG without creating an account. There are no download limits.' },
  { question: 'Can I use the gradients in commercial projects?', answer: 'Yes. These original gradient backgrounds are free for personal and commercial use, including websites, apps, presentations and client projects.' },
  { question: 'How do I add a gradient background to my website?', answer: 'Open a gradient, choose a colour variation and click Copy CSS. Paste the CSS into your stylesheet and apply its class to your element. If the CSS references an SVG file, download that SVG and update the background image path to match your project.' },
  { question: 'Which gradient format should I download?', answer: 'Use CSS for a website background, SVG for a scalable graphic, or PNG and JPEG for an image you can add to a design tool or presentation. PNG and JPEG downloads are 1920 × 1080 pixels; SVG can scale to fit your layout.' },
  { question: 'What is the difference between smooth, mesh and grain gradients?', answer: 'Smooth gradients blend colours softly. Mesh gradients combine several colour areas for a more organic background. Grain gradients add texture, while glow and wave collections offer light effects and flowing shapes. Browse the collections to find a style that suits your design.' },
  { question: 'Are there gradients for both light and dark mode?', answer: 'Yes. The collections include colour variations for light and dark designs. Use the Light or Dark tabs on a collection page or the All gradients page to narrow your choices.' },
  { question: 'Can I change the colours of a gradient?', answer: 'You can switch between the colour variations on a gradient’s details page. For further changes, edit the colour values in native gradient CSS or edit the downloaded SVG in a compatible design tool.' },
  { question: 'How do I switch gradients with a CSS class?', answer: 'Choose a template in How to use and copy its stylesheet link into your HTML head. Add fg-gradient and a colour class such as fg-aurora-01 to your element. Replace the colour class with another variation from the same template. Each stylesheet contains only one template; textured gradients load their required SVG automatically.' },
];
---
<section id="faq" class="section container faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="section-heading faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions.</h2>
    <p class="text-body-md">A little help with your next background.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    {questions.map(({ question, answer }) => <details class="faq-item">
      <summary class="text-body-md"><span>{question}</span><span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
      <div class="faq-answer text-body-md"><p>{answer}</p></div>
    </details>)}
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .faq-heading { text-align: center; }
  .faq-list { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); max-width: 800px; margin-inline: auto; }
  .faq-item { background: var(--surface-card); border-radius: var(--space-12); overflow: hidden; }
  .faq-item summary { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-8); padding: var(--space-12); cursor: pointer; list-style: none; color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium); }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item summary:focus-visible { outline-offset: -3px; border-radius: var(--space-12); }
  .faq-toggle-icon { position: relative; width: 20px; height: 20px; flex: 0 0 20px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .faq-toggle-icon::before, .faq-toggle-icon::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 9px 3px; height: 2px; border-radius: var(--radius-full); background: currentColor; }
  .faq-toggle-icon::after { transform: rotate(90deg); transition: transform 240ms ease, opacity 240ms ease; }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle-icon::after { transform: rotate(0deg); opacity: 0; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .faq-toggle-icon::after { transition: none; } }
  .faq-answer { padding: 0 var(--space-12) var(--space-12); color: var(--text-secondary); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (max-width: 639px) { .faq-item summary { padding: var(--space-8); } .faq-answer { padding: 0 var(--space-8) var(--space-8); } }
</style>
